<SiteLayout title="Movement Is Part Of Learning | Growing Kids" description="Explore movement activities at Growing Kids, from balancing to jumping, and ask your center how they fit into your child’s day." breadcrumbs={[{name:"Movement Is Part Of Learning",path:'/minds-in-motion/'}]}><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>Movement Is Part Of Learning</h1><p class="intro">The current Growing Kids website describes Minds in Motion as a course of movement activities such as crawling, rolling, balancing and jumping. Ask your center how these activities fit into your child’s classroom day.</p></div></section><section class="section cream"><div class="wrap reading"><h2>Room to move and explore.</h2><p>Movement activities give children ways to practice balance and coordination through play. Comfortable clothing and shoes help children take part.</p><p>Talk with your teacher about current activities. Exact schedules and availability should be confirmed with your center.</p><p><a href="/curriculum/">Explore ELM and Conscious Discipline</a></p><p><a href="/resource-policy-library/">Family resources</a> · <a href="/faqs/">Common questions</a> · <a href="/team/">Our team</a></p></div></section></SiteLayout>